       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (immediate-release, FDA labeling). A dose that high risks severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant 2,550 mg as the total daily dose. That would be **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals**.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n1. **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n2. A different dose or frequency, such as a lower starting dose (500 mg BID or 850 mg daily, then titrate)\n3. 2550 mg TID as written, if it's intentional. I'd need you to confirm that explicitly.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
