     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day, and I don't know of any clinical indication for that. It is well into the range associated with metformin toxicity and lactic acidosis, and the patient's normal kidney and liver function wouldn't protect against that. Because the order would go into the system and could be given, I'd rather not enter it than count on a downstream check catching it.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **A lower starting regimen**, such as 500 mg PO BID with meals, to titrate up\n\nIf you have a reason for going above the labeled maximum, the safer route is to talk to pharmacy or enter it directly through your institution's override process. That way a pharmacist can review it and document the rationale.\n\nTell me which of the two you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
